IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa29-sch2-part2.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 2, PART 2 "Specified descriptions of disclosures".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/gen_sch2.py (the Schedule's words are copied from the text by script; the short labels
-- and the sub-paragraph definitions are hand-written) and work/build.py (quote lines from srcrefs.py).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART DOES. Section 948(2) (coa21) bars the Takeover Panel from disclosing information about an individual's private affairs or a
-- business without that person's consent; s 948(3)(c) says the bar does not apply to a disclosure "of a description specified in Part 2 of
-- that Schedule". Part 2 is that list, in five groups: (A) United Kingdom, (B) Jersey, (C) Guernsey, (D) Isle of Man, (E) General.
-- One constructor stands for each paragraph, or for each lettered limb where the limbs name different Acts or bodies, or for each kind of
-- professional where one paragraph names several. The repealed paragraphs and limbs (A 18, A 25(b), (c), (h), (j), A 26, A 38, E 5) have
-- no constructor: they are blank in this text.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the disclosure is of a description the Part lists; JUST
-- FALSE = no description in the Part holds (s 948(3)(c) hands the question to the list: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a), a definition handed to a
-- list: when no head in the list holds, JUST FALSE); NOTHING = the answer rests on a meaning the Part borrows from another Act, or on a
-- designation made outside the sources, which is not known.

§ `Schedule 2 -- Part 2: specified descriptions of disclosures`

