-- The Schedule's own words for each description, copied from the text by script (a lettered limb is the paragraph's opening words and the limb).
@ref sch 2 Part 2 Specified descriptions of disclosures (src:19122-19322)
GIVEN description IS A `sch 2 part 2 description`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 2 part 2 the words of the description` MEANS
    CONSIDER description
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 1 a person authorised under section 457 of this Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person authorised under section 457 of this Act (revision of defective accounts: persons authorised to apply to court) to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 2 an inspector appointed under Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting an inspector appointed under Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (investigation of companies and their affairs, etc ) to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 3 a person authorised under section 447 of the Companies Act 1985 or section 84 of the Companies Act 1989` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person authorised under section 447 of the Companies Act 1985 (power to require production of documents) or section 84 of the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40) (exercise of powers by officer etc ) to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 4 a person appointed under section 167 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed under section 167 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) (general investigations) to conduct an investigation to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 5 a person appointed under section 168 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed under section 168 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (investigations in particular cases) to conduct an investigation to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 6 a person appointed under section 169(1)(b) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed under section 169(1)(b) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (investigation in support of overseas regulator) to conduct an investigation to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 7 the body corporate administering the ombudsman scheme (section 225 of the 2000 Act)` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the body corporate responsible for administering the scheme referred to in section 225 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (the ombudsman scheme) to exercise its functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 8 a person appointed under paragraph 4 or 5 of Schedule 17 to the 2000 Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed under paragraph 4 or 5 of Schedule 17 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (the panel of ombudsmen or the Chief Ombudsman) to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 9 a person appointed under regulations made under section 262(1) and (2)(k) of the 2000 Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed under regulations made under section 262(1) and (2)(k) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (investigations into open-ended investment companies) to conduct an investigation to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 10 a person appointed under section 284 of the 2000 Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed under section 284 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (investigations into affairs of certain collective investment schemes) to conduct an investigation to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 11 the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 (arrangements for investigation of complaints) to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 12 a person appointed by the Treasury to hold an inquiry into financial services` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed by the Treasury to hold an inquiry into matters relating to financial services (including an inquiry under section 69 of the Financial Services Act 2012) to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(a) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under the Companies Acts` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (a) the Companies Acts;"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(b) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under the Insolvency Act 1986` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (b) the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(c) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (c) the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (c. 46);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(d) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under Part 3 or 7 of the Companies Act 1989` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (d) Part 3 (investigations and powers to obtain information) or 7 (financial markets and insolvency) of the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(e) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under Part 5 of the Criminal Justice Act 1993` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (e) Part 5 of the Criminal Justice Act 1993 (c. 36) (insider dealing);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(f) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (f) the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000;"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 13(g) the Secretary of State or the Treasury - functions under Part 42 of this Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following— (g) Part 42 of this Act (statutory auditors)."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 14 the Scottish Ministers - functions under the enactments relating to insolvency` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Scottish Ministers to exercise their functions under the enactments relating to insolvency."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 15 the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland - powers under the enactments relating to companies or insolvency` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland to exercise any powers conferred on it by the enactments relating to companies or insolvency."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 16 a person appointed or authorised by that Department under the enactments relating to companies or insolvency` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a person appointed or authorised by the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland under the enactments relating to companies or insolvency to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 17 an official receiver (including the Accountant in Bankruptcy in Scotland and the Official Assignee in Northern Ireland)` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting an official receiver (including the Accountant in Bankruptcy in Scotland and the Official Assignee in Northern Ireland) to exercise their functions under the enactments relating to insolvency."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 19 a recognised professional body for the purposes of section 391 of the Insolvency Act 1986` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a body that is for the time being a recognised professional body for the purposes of section 391 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (recognised professional bodies) to exercise its functions as such."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 20(a) the Pensions Regulator - functions under the Pension Schemes Act 1993` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Pensions Regulator to exercise the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of any of the following— (a) the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (c. 48);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 20(b) the Pensions Regulator - functions under the Pensions Act 1995` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Pensions Regulator to exercise the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of any of the following— (b) the Pensions Act 1995 (c. 26);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 20(c) the Pensions Regulator - functions under the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Pensions Regulator to exercise the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of any of the following— (c) the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999 (c. 30);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 20(d) the Pensions Regulator - functions under the Pensions Act 2004` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Pensions Regulator to exercise the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of any of the following— (d) the Pensions Act 2004 (c. 35);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 20(e) the Pensions Regulator - functions under a corresponding enactment in force in Northern Ireland` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Pensions Regulator to exercise the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of any of the following— (e) any enactment in force in Northern Ireland corresponding to any of those enactments."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 21 the Board of the Pension Protection Fund` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Board of the Pension Protection Fund to exercise the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of Part 2 of the Pensions Act 2004 or any enactment in force in Northern Ireland corresponding to that Part."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 22 the Bank of England` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Bank of England to exercise its functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 23 the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs to exercise their functions."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 24 organs of the Society of Lloyd's` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting organs of the Society of Lloyd's (being organs constituted by or under the Lloyd's Act 1982 (c. xiv)) to exercise their functions under or by virtue of the Lloyd's Acts 1871 to 1982."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(a) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under the Fair Trading Act 1973` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (a) the Fair Trading Act 1973 (c. 41);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(d) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under the Competition Act 1980` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (d) the Competition Act 1980 (c. 21);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(e) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under the Competition Act 1998` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (e) the Competition Act 1998 (c. 41);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(f) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (f) the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(g) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under the Enterprise Act 2002` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (g) the Enterprise Act 2002 (c. 40);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(i) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under the Business Protection from Misleading Marketing Regulations 2008` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (i) the Business Protection from Misleading Marketing Regulations 2008 (S.I. 2008/1276);"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(k) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under Parts 3 and 4 of the Enterprise and Regulatory Reform Act 2013` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (k) Parts 3 and 4 of the Enterprise and Regulatory Reform Act 2013;"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(l) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under Schedule 3 to the Consumer Rights Act 2015` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (l) Schedule 3 to the Consumer Rights Act 2015"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(m)(i) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under Part 3 of the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (m) the following provisions of the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024— (i) Part 3;"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(m)(ii) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under Chapter 1 of Part 4 of the 2024 Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (m) the following provisions of the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024— (ii) Chapter 1 of Part 4;"
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 25(m)(iii) the Competition and Markets Authority - functions under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of the 2024 Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Competition and Markets Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following— (m) the following provisions of the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024— (iii) Chapter 2 of Part 5."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 27 proceedings before the Competition Appeal Tribunal` THEN "A disclosure with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, proceedings before the Competition Appeal Tribunal."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 28 an enforcer under Chapter 3 or 4 of Part 3 of the 2024 Act` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting an enforcer under Chapter 3 or 4 of Part 3 of the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024 (enforcement of consumer legislation) to exercise their functions under that Chapter."
    WHEN `sch 2 part 2(A) para 29 the Charity Commission` THEN "A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Charity Commission to exercise its functions."
