         AND (NOT (`the person has been admitted to the Bar under the Advocates and Solicitors (Jersey) Law 1997`))
         AND `the person is a member, and entitled to practise as such, of a legal profession regulated within a jurisdiction outside Jersey`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ foreign lawyer ” means a person who has not been admitted as mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) but is a member, and entitled to practise as such, of a legal profession regulated within a jurisdiction outside Jersey"

-- src:19250 | (2) In sub-paragraph (1) “ public servant ” means—
-- src:19251 | (a) an individual who holds office under, or is employed by, the Crown,
-- src:19252 | (b) a member, officer or employee of the States of Jersey or an officer or employee in an administration of the States of Jersey,
-- src:19253 | (c) a member, officer or employee of the Jersey Financial Services Commission, or
-- src:19254 | (d) any person exercising public functions who is declared by Order of the Minister for Economic Development to be a public servant for the purposes of paragraph 25 of the Schedule to the Companies (Takeovers and Mergers Panel) (Jersey) Law 2009.
@ref sch 2 part 2(B) para 13(2) Public servant (Jersey) (src:19250-19254)
GIVEN `the person is an individual who holds office under, or is employed by, the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member, officer or employee of the States of Jersey or an officer or employee in an administration of the States of Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member, officer or employee of the Jersey Financial Services Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises public functions and is declared by Order of the Minister for Economic Development to be a public servant for the purposes of paragraph 25 of the Schedule to the Companies (Takeovers and Mergers Panel) (Jersey) Law 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 part 2(B) para 13(2) the person is a public servant` MEANS
    IF       `the person is an individual who holds office under, or is employed by, the Crown`
         OR  `the person is a member, officer or employee of the States of Jersey or an officer or employee in an administration of the States of Jersey`
         OR  `the person is a member, officer or employee of the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
         OR  `the person exercises public functions and is declared by Order of the Minister for Economic Development to be a public servant for the purposes of paragraph 25 of the Schedule to the Companies (Takeovers and Mergers Panel) (Jersey) Law 2009`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In sub-paragraph (1) “ public servant ” means— (a) an individual who holds office under, or is employed by, the Crown, (b) a member, officer or employee of the States of Jersey or an officer or employee in an administration of the States of Jersey, (c) a member, officer or employee of the Jersey Financial Services Commission, or (d) any person exercising public functions who is declared by Order of the Minister for Economic Development to be a public servant"

